# CLEAR CLOSE K.1-K.4: MANUAL SETUP / TEST GUIDE
# Final completion is now connected; final-completion-manual.http supersedes the
# earlier stage's ACTIVE/APPROVED expectations and dormant completion description.
# No commands or tests in this guide were executed by the coding agent.
#
# AFFECTED APPLICATION
# Payment handling is inside clearclose-exit-service (8083), so its Kafka producer
# and exit consumer share one application. No separate payment service was added.
# Existing audit Kafka code in Grievance/Collateral/AuditService is unchanged.
# No schema/table migration or REST/security changes are required for Kafka.
# Only the paid-quote receipt visibility changed in the borrower frontend.
#
# CREATED FILES
# Root: compose.kafka.yml
# Exit Service Java:
#   config/KafkaEventConfig.java
#   events/PaymentEvent.java
#   events/PaymentEventProducer.java
#   events/PaymentEventConsumer.java
#   events/PaymentConfirmationService.java
#   events/LoanExitCompletedEvent.java
#   events/LoanExitEventProducer.java
# Exit Service: kafka-manual.http, kafka-verification.sql
# MODIFIED FILES
# Exit Service: pom.xml, src/main/resources/application.properties, .env.example,
#   payment/PaymentService.java, payment-manual.http, payment-verification.sql
# Frontend: src/pages/BorrowerDashboard.jsx (receipt stays visible for PAID quotes).
#
# TOPICS (declared by NewTopic beans; actually created when KafkaAdmin connects)
# clearclose.payment.succeeded       key = quoteId, JSON PaymentEvent version 1
# clearclose.loan-exit.completed     key = loanId, JSON LoanExitCompletedEvent v1
# clearclose.payment.succeeded.DLT   recoverable invalid/failed consumer messages
# Defaults: 3 partitions, replication factor 1 (local development only).
# Source and DLT must have matching partition counts. If reusing larger existing
# topics, set KAFKA_EVENT_PARTITIONS accordingly. No completion messages are sent.
#
# CONFIGURATION (set in the Java process environment/IDE, not Vite)
# KAFKA_BOOTSTRAP_SERVERS=localhost:9092
# PAYMENT_EVENT_GROUP=clearclose-exit-payment-v1   (keep stable across restarts)
# PAYMENT_EVENT_LISTENER_ENABLED=true
# KAFKA_EVENT_PARTITIONS=3
# KAFKA_EVENT_REPLICAS=1
# Spring Boot does not auto-load .env; .env.example is a reference template.
# Existing Razorpay credentials and JWT settings are not changed by this task.
#
# START LOCALLY (PowerShell, manually)
# Reuse your broker at localhost:9092 if it already exists. Otherwise from root:
#   docker compose -f compose.kafka.yml up -d
#   docker compose -f compose.kafka.yml ps
# This is a single-node KRaft development broker; no ZooKeeper is needed.
# Data/offsets persist in the named volume. Do not remove that volume for restart tests.
# Then from backend/clearclose-exit-service:
#   .\mvnw.cmd compile
#   .\mvnw.cmd spring-boot:run
# Or rebuild/restart com.clearclose.exit.ClearcloseExitServiceApplication in IDE.
# Keep existing discovery/auth/gateway/loan services running as usual.
# This guide intentionally asks YOU to compile/start; neither was run by the agent.
#
# LIST TOPICS (from repository root)
#   docker compose -f compose.kafka.yml exec kafka /opt/kafka/bin/kafka-topics.sh --bootstrap-server kafka:19092 --list
# KafkaAdmin declares all three topics at application startup when broker is up.
# If the app was started before Kafka, restart the app after Kafka is ready or
# create each topic manually using the following command with its actual name:
#   docker compose -f compose.kafka.yml exec kafka /opt/kafka/bin/kafka-topics.sh --bootstrap-server kafka:19092 --create --if-not-exists --topic clearclose.payment.succeeded --partitions 3 --replication-factor 1
# Repeat for clearclose.loan-exit.completed and clearclose.payment.succeeded.DLT.
# If using an existing non-Docker broker, use its bin scripts with localhost:9092.
#
# WATCH PAYMENT EVENTS (separate terminal, from repository root)
#   docker compose -f compose.kafka.yml exec kafka /opt/kafka/bin/kafka-console-consumer.sh --bootstrap-server kafka:19092 --topic clearclose.payment.succeeded --from-beginning --property print.key=true --property "key.separator=|"
# WATCH DLT (same command, --topic clearclose.payment.succeeded.DLT).
# Inspect DLT headers using --property print.headers=true for failure context.
# INSPECT COMPLETION TOPIC (must stay empty in ordinary payment flows):
#   docker compose -f compose.kafka.yml exec kafka /opt/kafka/bin/kafka-console-consumer.sh --bootstrap-server kafka:19092 --topic clearclose.loan-exit.completed --from-beginning --timeout-ms 10000
# A console timeout with no records is expected for the unused completion topic.
# INSPECT CONSUMER OFFSETS/LAG:
#   docker compose -f compose.kafka.yml exec kafka /opt/kafka/bin/kafka-consumer-groups.sh --bootstrap-server kafka:19092 --describe --group clearclose-exit-payment-v1
#
# PRODUCER FLOW
# Existing Razorpay capture verification updates PAYMENT to SUCCESS and writes
# PAYMENT_VERIFIED. PaymentEventProducer queries the verified DB record, generates
# UUID eventId and DB UTC occurredAt, then saves PAYMENT_EVENT_READY identity in
# AUDIT_LOG in that same transaction. A Spring AFTER_COMMIT listener sends JSON.
# Failed/authorized/unverified payments and rolled-back transactions emit nothing.
# Repeated verification/status calls on SUCCESS never run the transition again.
# Topic key is quoteId. Kafka producer idempotence, acks=all, retries=3 and a
# 15-second delivery deadline bound transient broker retries. max.block.ms=3000
# bounds waiting for metadata/buffer space on the payment HTTP thread.
# Publication failure is logged with eventId/paymentId/quoteId, without tokens,
# signatures, card details or credentials. It cannot roll back a captured payment.
#
# CONSUMER FLOW / DUPLICATES
# Fixed PaymentEvent JSON target; producer type headers are not trusted.
# Validate type/version, UUID, positive IDs, quoteId message key, INR, amount,
# timestamp and actual PAYMENT/QUOTE/LOAN/REQUEST joins. Payment must be SUCCESS,
# have provider ID and CONFIRMED_AT, and match PAYMENT_EVENT_READY identity/time.
# Lock the request then quote/payment rows, matching existing payment lock order.
# If PAYMENT_EVENT_CONFIRMED already exists for this payment, return without a
# second update/audit. Otherwise require APPROVED request + ACTIVE loan, change
# ACCEPTED quote to PAID, and insert PAYMENT_EVENT_CONFIRMED atomically.
# A crash after DB commit but before offset commit causes redelivery; the durable
# audit marker makes it harmless. Other payloads reusing an event ID are rejected
# unless they match both the original audit identity and verified DB relationships.
#
# CONSUMER FAILURES
# Non-retryable invalid contracts/deserialization go to DLT. Transient processing
# errors receive 2 retries separated by 2 seconds, then DLT. The DLT send must be
# broker-confirmed before the source offset can advance. If that send fails, the
# record remains unacknowledged and recovery is retried; it is not discarded.
# With RECORD ack mode + auto commit off, normal offsets commit only after the
# transactional processing method commits. Keep group ID and Kafka data stable.
# Recovery/DLT replays need operator review; there is no automatic DLT consumer.
#
# MANUAL HAPPY PATH
# 1. Use a fresh active loan and APPROVED request; generate/accept an unexpired quote.
# 2. Make a Razorpay TEST payment through the existing borrower dashboard.
# 3. Confirm PAYMENT SUCCESS and PAYMENT_EVENT_READY using kafka-verification.sql.
# 4. Watch a single PaymentSucceeded and the service log's CONFIRMED result.
# 5. Oracle should show quote PAID, loan ACTIVE, request APPROVED, and one
#    PAYMENT_EVENT_CONFIRMED audit. Refresh/reopen the quote to view the paid state.
# 6. Repeat the same signed verify request: no additional event/audit/payment.
# 7. Failed/cancelled/invalid-signature/authorized-only attempts must emit no event.
#
# DUPLICATE / INCORRECT DATA / MALFORMED TESTS
# Use kafka-verification.sql to get the original event as one quoteId|JSON line.
# Save that line locally to payment-event-replay.jsonl (UTF-8, no SQL column labels).
# From repository root, replay it manually:
#   Get-Content -LiteralPath .\payment-event-replay.jsonl | docker compose -f compose.kafka.yml exec -T kafka /opt/kafka/bin/kafka-console-producer.sh --bootstrap-server kafka:19092 --topic clearclose.payment.succeeded --property parse.key=true --property "key.separator=|"
# Repeating it must log DUPLICATE_IGNORED and leave exactly one confirmation audit.
# For rejection tests, copy that line and change amount, version, payment/quote ID,
# currency or eventId individually. Each invalid message must go to DLT and leave
# PAYMENT, quote, loan and request unchanged. Send quoteId|not-json to test malformed
# JSON; DLT must preserve the original bytes. Never test a dummy LoanExitCompleted.
# Fix/review the failure cause before replaying a DLT payload to the source topic.
#
# FAILURE / RESTART TESTS
# Because payment + exit share one app, stopping Exit Service also stops payment.
# To simulate the exit consumer being offline while payment stays available:
# restart the app with PAYMENT_EVENT_LISTENER_ENABLED=false, make a fresh Test Mode
# payment, confirm Kafka event and quote still ACCEPTED; restart with true and the
# SAME group ID, then verify pending event -> PAID exactly once.
# Stop/restart Kafka with docker compose -f compose.kafka.yml stop kafka / start kafka.
# Services should reconnect. If a payment was captured during broker downtime,
# PAYMENT remains SUCCESS. Wait for bounded send failure, then recover as below.
# Stop/restart the app during consumer processing and verify redelivery is harmless.
#
# MANUAL PUBLICATION RECOVERY / LIMITATIONS
# No transactional outbox existed and none was added. Oracle commit and Kafka
# acknowledgement are not atomic. A process crash after commit/before sending,
# or a send failure after retries, can leave SUCCESS with no event in Kafka.
# The existing audit log preserves identity and time for operator-driven recovery.
# kafka-verification.sql lists READY rows with no CONFIRMED row and builds exact
# replay JSON. Review Kafka backlog/DLT first, then replay with the producer command.
# Broker retries may themselves deliver duplicates; the consumer remains idempotent.
# Records only survive as long as broker retention/volume and Oracle audit history
# are retained. No automatic producer retry worker/backfill is implemented.
# Old SUCCESS payments without READY markers are not automatically published;
# use fresh test payments or design a separate reviewed legacy backfill.
# FUTURE PROPOSAL (not applied): a dedicated outbox with unique eventId, payload,
# status, attempts and created/published timestamps, inserted in the payment DB
# transaction and drained by a retrying worker. Consumers remain idempotent.
# This would require an explicit schema migration/review; no table SQL was added.
#
# LOAN EXIT COMPLETED -- PREPARED, NOT ACTIVATED
# LoanExitCompletedEvent + LoanExitEventProducer are configured, with no callers
# from payment/approval/startup and no listener in LoanAccount/Collateral/Audit.
# Future prepareAfterFinalCompletion(paymentId) requires a live DB transaction,
# verified SUCCESS payment, PAID quote, officer decision, COMPLETED request and
# CLOSED/EXIT_COMPLETED loan already confirmed in Oracle, then publishes after
# commit with loanId key. It does not perform any of those transitions itself.
# The future workflow must confirm LoanAccount's update and add durable publication
# and completion deduplication before wiring this method. Serialization can be
# inspected/tested locally without sending any completion event to the broker.
# Loan closure, request completion, NOC and collateral release are not implemented.
#
# OFFICIAL REFERENCES
# https://docs.spring.io/spring-kafka/reference/kafka/annotation-error-handling.html
# https://docs.spring.io/spring-kafka/reference/kafka/serdes.html
# https://kafka.apache.org/41/getting-started/docker/

@gateway = http://localhost:8080
@token = REPLACE_WITH_BORROWER_JWT
@quoteId = 2

### Existing endpoint: inspect the backend-confirmed payment
POST {{gateway}}/api/payments/quotes/{{quoteId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
